# Movement gallery

A change to how the playable cast or the crowd moves also updates `viewer/movement.html` in the same change.

That page is the check. Open it, click a person, play the clip, and run **Check cast and crowd**. Drag the view to orbit and scroll to zoom. A passing walk swings the hands and the feet, with the palms toward the thighs. A bind pose (arms out, legs straight) is a failure.

- The cast in the gallery is the game's avatar: `createPlayerAvatar(THREE, scene, { remember: false })` from `viewer/players.js`, driven by `avatar.update(dt, pos, speed, yaw, kind, deck)` exactly as `viewer/index.html` does. Speeds come from `MOVE` and `JUMP` in `viewer/player-motion.js` (Jog is the W speed, Run is Shift), and the jump uses the shared `stepJump`. The Velo and the step are placed with `placeRideVelo` (`viewer/velo.js`) and `placeRideScooter` / `scooterDeck` (`viewer/scooters.js`), the same calls the game makes. A grid scrolls at the speed, so a sliding foot shows. Fix a cast pose in `players.js` or the bake, never in the gallery.
- Cast clips: `viewer/characters/players/clips/{pieter,mo,jacob}_moves.glb` — Idle, Walk, Jog, Run, Jump, Punch, Cross, Kick, baked by `scripts/bake_player_locomotion.py -- swap` from the Mixamo FBX. The bake puts the wrists in shoulder space scaled by arm length, so elbows bend like the source on a longer Rocketbox torso. It sets each hand from the source's knuckle line (`hand_align`), then copies Mixamo's fingers and thumbs for every clip. Finger aim follows the next knuckle (or head→tail on the tip), not a fixed local axis, because the three-segment Biped fingers (Mo, Jacob) do not point +Y along the bone. A Mixamo distal fold on those long tip bones is capped with an axis-angle curl (~38°), not a right-angle kink — Pieter's two-segment tips keep a sharper fold.
- Punches and crosses are upper-body overlays (`players.js`): legs keep the walk/jog/run clip (legs-only tracks) while spine/arms play the strike. Kicks stay full-body. A jump that ends must leave `current` on its clip so the next gait crossfades it out.
- Cast Velo plays `{id}_Riding.glb`; the step plays `{id}_Scooter.glb`. Both preload in `build()`. Arm IK puts the wrists on the bars, `ride-lean.js` bends the back until they reach (above the pelvis on the step, so the planted feet stay), and the fingers close to 80% of the baked Punch fist. On a deck the root stands on the deck top, so the step grip height is measured from there.
- Crowd riders (bicycle, bakfiets, step) use the meshes from `viewer/micromobility.js` and `viewer/scooters.js` at their own size, with the rider on that frame's saddle, cranks, and bars. Gallery riders face +Z, so their left is +X. Seat the feet and hands in the vehicle's own axes: the Velo is yawed, and the step's grips are already flipped with the deck. The left pedal starts forward and travels downward.
- The Velo is `viewer/vehicles/velo.glb`, built in Blender by `scripts/build_velo_glb.py`. Its saddle, crank, and grip points come from empties in that file (`VELO_RIDE` in `viewer/velo.js`). The game and the gallery fold the rider's back toward the bars with the same `viewer/ride-lean.js`, so a pose change goes there once. Leg IK swings each bone toward its child: Pieter's legs run along local +Y, while Mo's and Jacob's Biped legs run along +X.
- `scripts/fix_coat_weights.py` hangs the cast's coats from the pelvis, so a raised thigh does not lift the back hem over the saddle. It also hangs Pieter's shirt tail (`SHIRT_TAILS`) fully from the pelvis, so it stays under the jacket. Run it again after re-exporting a `{id}_Walking.glb`.
- NPC bicycles and steps: `viewer/characters/clips/{Name}_Riding.glb` and `{Name}_Scooter.glb` on the Mixamo walking mesh. Spawned from `viewer/micromobility.js`.
- Crowd walks: the clip baked into each `viewer/characters/people/*.glb`, played from `viewer/people.js` and stepped in `viewer/pedestrians.js`.
- New clip names, a renamed file, or a different pass rule (how far a hand or foot must travel) go in `viewer/movement.html` as well as the game.
